---
import Guide from "../../layouts/Guide.astro";

const mistakes = [
  ["Closed before the work was finished",
    "The contractor's \"done\" closes the ticket automatically, while parts are still on order or a second visit is booked. Close the record when the work is finished, or keep it open with an open item that has an owner and a date."],
  ["No reply treated as yes",
    "The resident was sent a message and did not answer, and the job shows as confirmed. Silence is not a confirmation. Write \"no reply\", with the date you asked, and close for that reason if you have to."],
  ["A temporary fix closed as done",
    "A leak stopped with a clamp, a breaker reset, a part bypassed. These are often the right first step, but they are not the repair. Record them as a temporary fix and add what is left."],
  ["The symptom replaced by the diagnosis",
    "The record says \"replaced capacitor\" and nobody remembers that the resident reported a burning smell. Keep the reporter's words; the cause goes in the contractor's statement."],
  ["\"Checked\" without saying how",
    "\"Checked OK\" could mean a full test or a glance from the door. Say who checked, how, what they found, and what they did not cover."],
  ["A photo taken as proof of quality",
    "A photo of a new pipe joint shows a new pipe joint. It does not show that the joint holds, or that it was the right fix. Note what each photo shows, and never refuse a report just because it has none."],
  ["Earlier entries overwritten",
    "The first visit's notes are edited when the second visit finds something else, and the history disappears. Add new entries. If a closed record reopens, keep the earlier closure as it was."],
  ["Asking a resident about a common area",
    "Nobody lives in the plant room. For common areas, the resident's answer is \"not applicable\", and the check matters more."],
];
---
<Guide
  path="/guide/mistakes/"
  title="Common mistakes in repair completion reports"
  description="Closed before the work was finished, no reply treated as yes, a temporary fix closed as done, and five more."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">The guide</p>
  <h1>Common mistakes</h1>
  <p class="lead">Eight ways a "completed" job ends up meaning less than it says. Each one is easy to avoid once it has a name.</p>
  {mistakes.map(([title, text], i) => (
    <section>
      <h3>{i + 1}. {title}</h3>
      <p>{text}</p>
    </section>
  ))}
  <div class="callout">
    <p>The <a href="/build/">builder's check</a> looks for most of these as you type: a closure that says "confirmed" while the resident never answered, a temporary fix with nothing left open, a check with no result.</p>
  </div>
</Guide>
